# ORCLBEAST: the seekers, and what touching one costs (M16.5).
#
# Every creature in this world reaches the player by a path that is free of
# random draws even though the draws still happen, which is how M16.4 handled
# the spinning gun and is the only honest way to compare a creature against
# vanilla at all. Two facts do the work (GAME.PAS CalcDirectionSeek):
#
#   if (Random(2) < 1) or (Board.Stats[0].Y = y) then deltaX := Signum(...)
#   if deltaX = 0 then deltaY := Signum(...)
#
# A creature standing in the player's ROW takes the first branch whatever the
# draw returns, and a creature in the player's COLUMN gets Signum(0) = 0 from it
# either way and falls through to the second. So seeking is deterministic on
# both axes as long as the creature and the player share one — and NOT otherwise,
# which is why the whole charge happens down row 13 and why the player never
# leaves that row while anything is hunting them.
#
# The gate in front of the seek is forced the same way: a lion, tiger or shark
# with P1 9 can never satisfy `P1 < Random(10)` (the draw tops out at 9), so it
# always seeks; a ruffian with P1 8 always satisfies `Random(9) <= P1`. Bears
# draw nothing at all.
#
# Claw Bay, row 13 — the charge lane, west to east:
#   12,13  Ruffian (cycle 1, P1 8, P2 9, step west). P2 9 is the other forced
#          draw: `(P2 + 8) <= Random(17)` can never hold, so this ruffian never
#          rests once moving and never wakes once stopped. It reaches the player
#          first and attacks, which kills it — a creature that lands a hit is
#          destroyed by its own BoardAttack (GAME.PAS:1224 DamageStat).
#   20,13  Lion (cycle 2, P1 9). Same charge, half the speed.
#   26,13  Breakable, and 30,13 a Bear (cycle 3, P1 8). The bear is the only
#          creature whose attack branch accepts something other than the player
#          (ELEMENTS.PAS ElementBearTick tests E_PLAYER or E_BREAKABLE), so it
#          spends itself on the wall and never reaches the player. P1 8 also
#          pins its sensitivity to `Difference(Y, playerY) <= 0`: it moves only
#          along the player's own row.
#
# 10,10 — the ruffian that never wakes. Its authored step is north into the
#   solid at 10,9, so its first tick zeroes the step; from then on it is in the
#   resting branch, where P2 9 makes the wake test unsatisfiable. It ticks
#   forever without moving, which is what makes it safe to walk up to it off
#   row 13. The player then touches it: ElementDamagingTouch attacks on the
#   player's behalf, so the ruffian dies and the player pays the same 10 health
#   as if it had charged (GAME.PAS BoardAttack, attackerStatId 0).
#
# 18,3 — the sensitivity bear (P1 4). Out of range for the whole charge and for
#   the walk to the resting ruffian; it wakes only when the player stands at
#   14,13, four columns from its own. Its route is the proof that both of
#   ElementBearTick's branches are being taken: it descends its column while
#   `Difference(Y, playerY)` is still over 4, turns west along row 9 the moment
#   that difference closes, and drops down the player's own column at the end.
#
# Health is the compared counter throughout: 100 -> 90 (ruffian) -> 80 (lion)
# -> 70 (touching the resting ruffian) -> 60 (the sensitivity bear). Nothing in
# this world can reach 0; death is the mp-respawn deviation, not vanilla, and is
# pinned by TestSinglePlayerDeathIsRespawnDeviation, never by an oracle capture.
world ORCLBEAST
seed 0
phase
boot 240
capture title
play
# Beast Hub: unpause and cross the east border opening at 60,13.
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
capture arrive
# The charge is already under way: the ruffian is the fast one.
settle 12
capture charge
settle 20
capture ruffian-hit
settle 24
capture lion-closing
settle 24
capture lion-hit
# Walk east to the resting ruffian's column, then up to it.
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move up
move up
move up
capture ruffian-touched
# Back down to row 13 and east to 14,13, where the sensitivity bear wakes.
move down
move down
move down
move right
move right
move right
move right
capture bear-waking
settle 40
capture bear-descending
settle 60
capture bear-hit
